---
source: crates/aozora-cli/tests/snapshot_cli.rs
expression: "run(&[\"completions\", \"--help\"])"
---
Print a shell completion script (`bash` / `zsh` / `fish` / `powershell` / `elvish` / `nushell`) on
stdout. Generated from the live command tree, so it always matches the installed binary; release
tarballs also ship these under `completions/`

Usage: aozora completions [OPTIONS] <SHELL>

Arguments:
  <SHELL>
          Shell dialect to emit a completion script for
          
          [possible values: bash, elvish, fish, powershell, zsh, nushell]

Options:
      --color <WHEN>
          When to colourise diagnostics: `auto` (colour on a terminal, honouring `NO_COLOR` /
          `CLICOLOR` / `CLICOLOR_FORCE`), `always`, or `never`. Global — accepted after any
          subcommand. Governs `check`'s graphical diagnostics; `kinds` tables are always monochrome

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Colour when stdout is a terminal (honours `NO_COLOR` / `CLICOLOR` /
            `CLICOLOR_FORCE`)
          - always: Always colour, even when piped
          - never:  Never colour
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
